### 🔧 Compiling a function exercise

Functions are compiled with a test `main.c` (and `ft_putchar.c` when needed):

```bash
cc -Wall -Wextra -Werror ft_putchar.c exXX/ft_function.c main.c -o test
./test
```

### 💻 Compiling a program exercise (`ex18`, `ex19`)

```bash
cc -Wall -Wextra -Werror ft_putchar.c exXX/ft_program.c -o a.out
./a.out arg1 arg2 arg3
```

### 🐚 Running a shell exercise

```bash
cd ex03
chmod +x find_sh.sh
./find_sh.sh | cat -e
```

### 📚 `ex24` – Static library

From the exercise directory (containing `srcs/` and `includes/`):

```bash
make          # builds libft.a
make clean    # removes object files
make fclean   # removes object files and libft.a
make re       # fclean + all
```

### 📄 `ex27` – `ft_display_file`

```bash
cd ex27
make
./ft_display_file file.txt
make fclean
```

| Situation | Message (standard error) |
|-----------|--------------------------|
| No argument | `File name missing.` |
| More than one argument | `Too many arguments.` |
| File cannot be read | `Cannot read file.` |

